uccess","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"d89e82229ea09620721c5351b1360d4d55ab05db0ff323f40a20f8c4252abd4a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":110852,"output_tokens":3130,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f78f6aca6e057514aaeb92d817bb3c92bf63fdf97756d32be8ef1e0a5b475ff0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T10","usage":{"input_tokens":184806,"output_tokens":3846,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the observability contract for the new internet-facing /mcp endpoint beyond liveness: name a metric/alarm (or an explicit justification for none) covering auth-failure and 5xx/502 rate, consistent with the sibling services' CloudWatch alarms.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '/health on the MCP server exposing an integer in_flight gauge ... The gauge feeds foxterrier's retire check; it does not gate the deploy.'","Plan Compat/rollback: 'new authenticated endpoint — static bearer at /mcp + TLS at the nginx edge'","compose mcp service declares only a liveness healthcheck + journald logging; no alarm is named for /mcp auth-failure or 5xx rate","ABSENCE: the plan names no monitoring resource for the new endpoint though sibling services have alarms (monitoring_eb6e.tf, monitoring_autodeploy.tf) referenced elsewhere in the compose file"],"finding":"The new internet-reachable authenticated `/mcp` endpoint has a liveness contract (/health gauge, container HEALTHCHECK, `docker compose ps` health, journald logging) but the plan specifies no alarm/metric on request errors or auth failures for it, unlike the sibling services which carry dedicated CloudWatch alarms (e.g. the review-bot's monitoring_eb6e.tf client-error alarm, monitoring_autodeploy.tf disk-pressure alarms).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90eeb5c0a58ec5fd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (/health gauge) + Compat/rollback (Trust boundary); docker-compose.yml mcp service healthcheck/logging","norm_id":"nea7577f5a97e595a","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A misconfigured bearer store or upstream flip that leaves /mcp returning 401/502 to real callers goes unnoticed because only container liveness (which stays green) is monitored","A credential-stuffing / brute-force pattern against the internet-facing /mcp bearer produces no alertable signal"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS is env-overridable (with 1200 as the default) or justify the hardcoded-constant choice, and pin the compose stop_grace_period ≥ constant invariant so the two cannot drift.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'_mcp_health.py defines DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200 (a module constant ... not a rebar config key)'","compose stop_grace_period 1260s is coupled to this value structurally"],"finding":"DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS is a hardcoded module constant (1200) with no override path, yet it is a threshold likely to evolve as op-duration profiles change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdb5a0185cd2fac0b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers)' + '/health' scope bullet","norm_id":"na1382634ac11db86","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future op class runs longer than 1200s and the grace must be raised without a code edit + redeploy","stop_grace_period and the constant drift apart if one is edited without the other"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Keep 1200 as the default but allow an env override (e.g. REBAR_MCP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS), and keep the existing structural AC that asserts stop_grace_period ≥ the effective constant.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the grace loop's poll interval and that the SIGTERM test drives in_flight→0 quickly (asserting the 1200s ceiling structurally, not by real-time waiting) so the test is in-session runnable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6429,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a SIGTERM does NOT exit immediately and exits 0 once the gauge drains, within the 1200s bound'","No stated poll interval or test-time gauge-release mechanism"],"finding":"The SIGTERM-grace AC asserts the handler 'exits 0 once the gauge drains, within the 1200s bound' but does not state the grace poll interval or how the test drains the gauge quickly, so an executor cannot tell whether the test must actually wait up to 1200s (not in-session feasible) or release the gauge fast against a large ceiling.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7b9f8f86b614f0e6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — SIGTERM grace line; Testing section","norm_id":"n8f82d88d53835e03","priority":0.1571,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor writes a test that blocks on the real 1200s ceiling and it times out CI","Ambiguity about whether the ceiling is asserted by waiting vs structurally"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State: the handler polls in_flight on a short interval (e.g. 1s); the test holds in_flight>0, sends SIGTERM, asserts non-exit, then releases the gauge and asserts exit 0 within seconds — the 1200s ceiling is asserted numerically against the constant, not by waiting.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the only-if-absent flip-seam contract and the new REBAR_MCP_* env surface in the ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur) or an infra README note so operators/foxterrier maintainers rely on a durable doc, not plan prose.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'copies the committed seed to /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf ONLY IF absent (so a foxterrier flip is never clobbered on redeploy)'","New env-var surface and a switchable-upstream flip seam consumed by foxterrier"],"finding":"The only-if-absent semantics of materialize-mcp-upstream.sh (why a redeploy must never clobber a foxterrier flip) is a novel operational/security-relevant seam described only in plan prose, with no operator-facing doc/ADR note beyond the referenced ADR.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f79cd35d3002df34c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — materialize-mcp-upstream.sh; 'nginx switchable upstream' section","norm_id":"n18fc1ff974272d20","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator runs a redeploy and expects the seed to reset the upstream but it silently preserves the green pointer","A future maintainer removes the only-if-absent guard not knowing it protects live flips"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify atomic/thread-safe mutation of the in_flight counter (lock or atomic primitive) and a drain check that has no check-then-act window with op acceptance, so SIGTERM never exits mid-op.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'exposing an integer in_flight gauge counting ONLY certified ops'","'On SIGTERM the process waits up to 1200s for in_flight to reach 0, then exits'","ABSENCE: no statement that the counter is mutated under a lock or via an atomic/thread-safe primitive, and no statement on how concurrent op start/finish interleave with the drain check"],"finding":"The in_flight gauge is mutable in-process shared state read/written by concurrent request handlers (increment on op start, decrement on completion) AND read by the SIGTERM grace handler that exits once it 'reaches 0'. The plan does not specify atomic mutation (lock/atomic counter) nor guard against a TOCTOU race where the handler observes 0 between a decrement and a not-yet-started concurrent op, or where concurrent increments/decrements interleave and lose an update.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa5770212745a8e92","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"/health gauge + SIGTERM grace sections; src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","norm_id":"na40fb779f9b6a43a","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two certified ops finish and start near-simultaneously; a non-atomic read-modify-write on the counter loses an update, so the gauge under- or over-counts and either the handler exits with work still in flight or never drains","SIGTERM handler reads in_flight==0 in a check-then-act window while a request handler is about to increment for an op just accepted, causing the process to exit mid-op despite the grace intent"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Back the gauge with a lock-guarded counter (or threading primitive) in _mcp_health.py, gate op acceptance and the SIGTERM drain check under the same lock so the drain-to-zero decision is race-free, and add a concurrency test that starts/finishes overlapping certified ops.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"loca